lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>YP 3.1.10 was =
released<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l2 level1 =
lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Next week is feature freeze for =
YP 3.4<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l2 level1 =
lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Known pending work for YP 3.4 =
includes rust support in core and the prserv =
changes.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l2 level1 =
lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>OE-Core has moved to the new =
override syntax and is now only compatible with the honister release =
series. Other layers will need to migrate to the new syntax to work with =
it. There is documentation about handling migration to the new syntax in =
the migration section of the manual:<o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><p =
style=3D'mso-margin-top-alt:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin=
-left:.5in'><a =
href=3D"http://docs.yoctoproject.org/migration-guides/migration-3.4.html#=
override-syntax-changes"><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:#1155CC'>http://docs.yoctop=
roject.org/migration-guides/migration-3.4.html#override-syntax-changes</s=
pan></a><o:p></o:p></p><ul =
style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There continue to be small bug =
fixes from the override syntax change but most of the core layers tested =
on the autobuilder now seem to be working ok.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We merged the upgrade to glibc =
to 2.34. Unfortunately this version makes some changes which have broken =
uninative and pseudo. Fixes for those issues are being =
investigated.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Kernel changes to drop 5.4 and =
switch to 5.10 and 5.13 are pending, mainly on other layers being ready =
for the change to the default versions.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There also appear to be issues =
in the buildtools tarball on aarch64, probably from the gcc 11 =
upgrade.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There is a plan to migrate the =
tune files into architecture specific directories. This patch will =
likely merge in the next few days and will need BSP layers to be updated =
as the tune files will no longer be found.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The bitbake fetcher no longer =
ignores SSL certificates by default (this wasn&#8217;t a huge problem as =
we separately checksum input files).<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>LTO linker flags handling =
changes were merged now the reproducibility issues it introduced were =
fixed meaning LTO builds should be more =
reproducible.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Overlayfs class changes were =
merged.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Intermittent issues are ongoing =
and help is very much welcome on these issues. You can see the list of =
failures we&#8217;re continuing to see by searching for the =
&#8220;AB-INT&#8221; tag in bugzilla: <a =
href=3D"https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?quicksearch=3DAB-IN=
T"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?qui=
cksearch=3DAB-INT</span></a><o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><p =
class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>Ways to =
